<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Basis firm as supplies tighten.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Basis firm as supplies tighten.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis levels for rail soymeal were firm on Monday amid signs that nearby supplies have tightened, dealers in the U.S. Midwest said.</p>
<p>&quot;The pipeline is pretty much cleaned up right now,&quot; one Indiana based dealer said.</p>
<p>Dealers noted talk that a leading Illinois processor was not offering any meal for the rest of January and was even bidding for supplies.</p>
<p>Last week's storms and cold weather also slowed the crushing pace in states such as Minnesota.  </p>
